    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense faces a volatile slate today, anchored by **Gunnar Henderson**, who earns our highest efficiency score of 81.88. His massive projection against Civale is fueled by a confluence of favorable variables: a 16% park boost, a 14% platoon edge, and the critical leadoff spot. Close behind him, **Kyle Tucker** (75.90) and **Jackson Merrill** (74.04) represent elite starts despite facing high-strikeout arms. **Kyle Tucker** benefits significantly from a 17% SP skill adjustment against the hard-throwing Strider, while **Jackson Merrill** remains a priority for his speed profile and a robust 13% platoon advantage against May. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (73.10) also commands a premium start in the UTIL slot, as his profile against Kochanowicz is bolstered by a 19% SP skill correction, making him an ideal anchor for RBI production.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Miguel Vargas**, who finished with a respectable 54.01 score but ultimately lost out to the superior efficiency of **Josh Lowe** and **Coby Mayo**. While **Miguel Vargas** offers a decent floor, the optimizer favored **Josh Lowe**'s 14% platoon advantage against Yesavage, despite the lower batting order spot. We are monitoring \"Lineup Pending\" statuses closely for **Drake Baldwin**, **Kyle Tucker**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Andy Pages**, and **Jackson Merrill**; should these projections fluctuate upon official confirmation, we remain prepared to pivot. Be advised that **Liam Hicks** carries the most risk in the starting nine; his 41.84 score is suppressed by a difficult 11% platoon penalty against Lovelady, marking him as a marginal start who is on the bubble of being benched to preserve our limited game caps.",
